=CE=94W</em><span> also contains 7B parameters, and computing the matrix </=
span><em>=CE=94W</em><span> can be very compute and memory intensive.</span=
></p><p><span>The LoRA method proposed by </span><a href=3D"https://arxiv.o=
rg/abs/2106.09685">Hu </a><em><a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.09685">=
et al.</a></em><span> replaces to decompose the weight changes, </span><em>=
=CE=94W</em><span>, into a lower-rank representation. To be precise, it doe=
s not require to explicitly compute </span><em>=CE=94W</em><span>. Instead,=
 LoRA learns the decomposed representation of </span><em>=CE=94W</em><span>=
 directly during training which is where the savings are coming from, as sh=
