mber of trainable LoRA parameters, the dataset can also influence memory us=
age.</p><p>Note that Llama 2 has a block size of 4048. For instance, if an =
LLM has a block size of 4048 tokens, it can process sequences of up to 4048=
 tokens at once. However, shorter training sequences can result in substant=
ial memory savings due to the masking of future tokens.</p><p>For example, =
the Alpaca dataset is relatively small, with a maximum length of 1304 token=
s.</p><div class=3D"captioned-image-container"><figure><a target=3D"_blank"=
